Subject: [PATCH 30/38] fate/source: Add old hevc headers to copyright &
 inclusion lists

Add old hevc header to exclusion lists rather than fixing them as
they are simple copies of system headers. Remove this patch once
we remove the old variation from the decoder.
---
 tests/ref/fate/source | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/ref/fate/source b/tests/ref/fate/source
index d5eb31d887e..61de8f16ce9 100644
--- a/tests/ref/fate/source
+++ b/tests/ref/fate/source
@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@
 Files without standard license headers:
 libavcodec/file_open.c
+libavcodec/hevc-ctrls-v1.h
+libavcodec/hevc-ctrls-v2.h
+libavcodec/hevc-ctrls-v3.h
 libavcodec/interplayacm.c
 libavcodec/log2_tab.c
 libavcodec/reverse.c
@@ -28,6 +31,9 @@ compat/float/float.h
 compat/float/limits.h
 compat/stdbit/stdbit.h
 libavcodec/bitstream_template.h
+libavcodec/hevc-ctrls-v1.h
+libavcodec/hevc-ctrls-v2.h
+libavcodec/hevc-ctrls-v3.h
 libswscale/x86/uops_macros.asm.h
 tools/decode_simple.h
 Use of av_clip() where av_clip_uintp2() could be used:
